  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Nave",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Nave\"**\n\nThe church as a cultural institution in print: an editorial publication you walk through like a nave, cover first. Pages are warm ivory paper with stone alternates; the cover, live worship and the close of every page sit in charcoal night fields; one deep forest green is the committed colour field. Instrument Serif sets the headlines large, at its single weight, with italic turns; Manrope carries everything that is read or operated. Bronze and champagne appear only as hairlines, dates, marks and active indicators.\n\nDensity is generous on the public site (section padding scales from 72px to 144px, more air above a heading than below) and efficient in the admin dashboard, which uses the same palette and type with standard controls: a forest rail, ivory work surface on a stone ground, Instrument Serif page titles and Manrope semibold for every small UI title. The frame is brand-neutral and light-only by product commitment: each church's own photographs and name lead, and nothing in the system assumes one congregation's colours. There is no dark mode.\n\nMotion is one orchestrated grammar, not a collection of effects: headings rise word by word from behind masks, image frames unveil from their bottom edge while the photo settles, hairlines draw across, content rises into place. Everything eases out exponentially and everything stands still under reduced motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm ivory page, stone alternates, charcoal night fields, one forest field.",
      "Instrument Serif headlines at weight 400 only; Manrope for text and UI.",
      "Bronze and champagne as hairlines and marks, never as surfaces.",
      "Square corners (1 to 8px); round only for dots, avatars and round icon buttons.",
      "Lists of entries as hairline-ruled rows, not card grids.",
      "Flat surfaces; shadow only on floating layers (modal, menus, toasts).",
      "One motion grammar: masked word rise, clip-path unveil, hairline draw, rise."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Metal Rule",
        "body": "Bronze and champagne are for marks, dates, active states and hairlines. They are never a resting fill for a rectangular button, a section background or body text. Champagne may appear as a hover state (the light button's wipe, a round play button) because that is an active state.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Field Rule",
        "body": "Large colour fields are night, forest or stone. Forest is the only committed chromatic field; no other hue takes a full section.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Light Only Rule",
        "body": "One light scheme on both the public site and the admin. No dark mode, no scheme toggle.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Single Weight Rule",
        "body": "Instrument Serif ships one weight. It is set at 400 and font synthesis is off; never bold or semibold a serif. Emphasis in a headline is the italic turn.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sans For Small Titles Rule",
        "body": "Below about 20px, a UI title is Manrope semibold, not the serif.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Kicker Rule",
        "body": "Nothing sits above a heading as a small tracked label. Small tracked capitals are marginalia and metadata only; tags and categories go after a title, never before it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ruled Rows Rule",
        "body": "A collection of entries is a ruled list, not a grid of cards. Image tiles in a gallery are the exception; text entries never are.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Rule",
        "body": "Resting surfaces have no shadow. If it does not float above the page, it does not cast.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Pill Rule",
        "body": "Nothing rectangular is pill-shaped. A tag, badge, button or chip keeps its 2px corner.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set every Instrument Serif headline at weight 400 and use the italic turn for emphasis.",
      "Do use Manrope semibold for small UI titles in the admin (modal titles, card headings).",
      "Do set entries as hairline-ruled rows with the date or thumbnail in a fixed lead column.",
      "Do keep large fields to ivory, stone, night and forest.",
      "Do use bronze on ivory and champagne on night or forest for dates, marks, active states and hairlines.",
      "Do keep corners between 1 and 8px; round only for dots, avatars, the seal and round icon buttons.",
      "Do give numbers tabular, lining figures.",
      "Do use the editorial note for public empty states and the empty-state block in the admin.",
      "Do run every reveal through the one grammar (masked word rise, unveil, rule, rise) with exponential ease-out, and respect reduced motion.",
      "Do declare `navOverlay: true` on any page that opens on a full-bleed cover so the navbar sits transparent over it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't bold or semibold Instrument Serif, or let the browser synthesise a bold.",
      "Don't put a small tracked label, kicker or eyebrow above a heading; tags and categories follow the title.",
      "Don't lay out text entries as a grid of cards.",
      "Don't fill a rectangular button, a section or body text with bronze or champagne.",
      "Don't make anything rectangular pill-shaped.",
      "Don't use a thick coloured side stripe on cards, alerts or list items; the only side mark is the 1px bronze margin rule on a page header or entry panel.",
      "Don't use gradient text, glass panels or hard offset shadows; shadow only for floating layers.",
      "Don't add a dark mode or bake one church's colours into the frame.",
      "Don't introduce a second motion vocabulary (bounces, springs, spins) beside the grammar."
    ]
  }
